{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the surgery team doctors. I understand you’re here because of increasing pain at your G-tube site. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been getting worse over the last few days. It’s a deep, constant ache right where the tube comes out. I was in the pain clinic yesterday, and they said it might be inflammation from the tube itself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That matches what we’re seeing. Your CT scan shows some inflammation in the muscle around the tube, but no abscess or infection. We’ve seen this before—it’s a reaction to the presence of the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:19:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I already had the tube changed recently, and it didn’t help. Why is it still hurting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:20:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes the tissue becomes sensitized, and even a new tube can cause irritation. We tried injecting a steroid through the tube earlier, but you didn’t get much relief, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, it only helped a little for a few hours. Is there anything else we can do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, we’re focusing on pain control. We’ve switched you from oxycodone to dilaudid by mouth, which seems to be working better. How’s the pain now, on a scale from 1 to 10?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s about a 5 now. That’s much better than earlier—thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:24:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep that going as needed. You’re still on continuous tube feeds at 40 cc/hr, and we tried giving a bolus earlier, but your blood sugar dropped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I felt shaky and weak. I’ve had that before—my hypoglycemia kicks in fast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:26:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. So we’ve gone back to continuous feeds to keep your sugars stable. We’ll send you home on NutriHep at 50 cc/hour. You’ll need to keep checking your blood sugar regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:27:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can do that. But what about the tube? The pain clinic said it might need to be removed or replaced."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2173-08-26 21:28:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s something to discuss with your surgeon. Right now, removing it isn’t urgent since there’s no infection. But if the pain continues, we may need to consider it. For now, we’re managing the inflammation and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You made it through the night well—vitals are stable, no fever, and your pain has been controlled. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Will I still have the pain at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have dilaudid to take as needed every 4 hours. If the pain isn’t improving within a day or gets worse, please call your surgeon or come back. Also, watch for fever, redness, or drainage at the site."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll keep the feeds going continuously and check my sugars?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Continue all your regular medications too, unless told otherwise. You have a follow-up with your surgeon soon—we’ll go over next steps then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2173-08-27 10:12:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Just take it easy, stay hydrated, and don’t drive while on the pain meds. We’ll get your discharge papers ready shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave—we reviewed your discharge instructions. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, everything’s clear. I’ll follow up with my surgeon and keep an eye on my symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care, and don’t hesitate to reach out if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:26:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your prescriptions and discharge paperwork now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2173-08-27 14:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready when she is."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2173-08-26 20:57:00",
    "admission_end": "2173-08-27 17:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with worsening pain at her G-tube site, persistent despite a recent tube exchange and prior steroid injection. Imaging showed inflammatory changes around the tube without abscess or infection. Pain was initially managed with oxycodone but transitioned to oral hydromorphone (dilaudid) with improved control. A trial of bolus tube feeds was unsuccessful due to hypoglycemia, so she was maintained on continuous feeds. The patient remained stable, afebrile, and hemodynamically normal throughout the stay. She was discharged home on continuous tube feeds (NutriHep at 50 cc/hr), dilaudid for breakthrough pain, and instructions to monitor blood glucose and follow up with her surgeon.",
    "problems": [
      "Other gastrostomy complications",
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption",
      "Nausea alone",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
